---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Juan Lopez — Behavior Analyst"
  description="Juan Lopez is a behavior analyst, researcher, and digital systems designer working across care, research, websites, commerce, and data."
  image="/images/portraits/about-observation-systems.webp"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-shell page-hero__inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Behavior Analyst, Researcher and Digital Systems Designer.</h1>
      <p class="page-hero__lede">
        Juan Lopez studies how environments, information, and experiences affect people, then carries that understanding into clearer, more humane systems.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section--tight">
    <div class="page-shell about-preview">
      <div class="about-preview__visual">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/images/portraits/about-observation-systems.avif" type="image/avif" />
          <source srcset="/images/portraits/about-observation-systems.webp" type="image/webp" />
          <img src="/images/portraits/about-observation-systems.webp" width="1200" height="1500" alt="Research notebook and paper layers arranged on a light surface" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        </picture>
      </div>
      <div class="about-preview__content">
        <p class="eyebrow">A shared foundation</p>
        <h2>Observation and implementation belong together.</h2>
        <p>
          Behavior analysis is Juan's primary lens. It brings careful observation, repeated measurement, individualized context, and socially meaningful outcomes into the same conversation.
        </p>
        <p>
          Research, web development, Shopify theme work, e-commerce, and information design are extensions of that foundation. They are ways to make environments clearer—not tactics for manipulating people.
        </p>
        <p>
          Across independent client work, Juan has handled strategy, information architecture, visual design, development, responsive implementation, content structure, forms, business email, payments, domain configuration, and launch.
        </p>
        <p>
          He is completing FIU degrees in Psychology on the Applied Behavior Analysis track and Natural and Applied Sciences. His current credentials include Registered Behavior Technician certification and CITI Social/Behavioral Human Research training.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="page-shell principles-grid">
      <article class="principle-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research</p>
        <h2>Questions with boundaries</h2>
        <p>Juan's Fall 2025 AI Misattribution project used an online experiment, Qualtrics, and IBM SPSS to test how source expectations affect social evaluation.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Client systems</p>
        <h2>Complete website delivery</h2>
        <p>SitePad projects show end-to-end work for service businesses, including forms, email, payments, responsive design, domains, and launch.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="principle-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Commerce</p>
        <h2>Shopify theme development</h2>
        <p>World Cup Items and VX Nexus demonstrate independent theme development, merchandising, art direction, commerce setup, and responsive storefront work.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
